rwtest 1
test "Dark mirage is refused out of range" project="Bernael" group="Ability" created=2026-09-21T00:00:00

# This file is the proof for the second half of the 2026-09-21 finding: that
# nothing in the kit could see an ability's range. It does not measure the
# number - "Abyssal reach lengthens a psycast" does that with
# "assert ability ... range". This one proves that the game itself turns an
# out-of-range aim down, and it proves it through the route a player takes.
#
# "cast" is not that route. It calls Ability.Activate directly, which runs
# PreActivate and ApplyEffects and nothing else - no verb, no warmup, no job
# and no range. The route the game uses is two steps, and both are verbs this
# kit already had:
#
#   gizmo "Dark mirage"     Command_Ability.ProcessInput -> Targeter.BeginTargeting
#   target cell=...         the map click -> Verb_CastAbility.ValidateTarget
#
# ValidateTarget asks Verb.CanHitTarget first, and on a no it posts
# "AbilityOutOfRange" and keeps asking for a target. That is what expect=refused
# reads: the targeter is still open after the click. No logic of vanilla is
# mirrored here, so nothing in this file goes stale when Ludeon moves the gate.
#
# BX_DarkMirage carries verbProperties range 19.9 and requireLineOfSight, and
# the pawn is a plain colonist without BX_AbyssalReach, so 19.9 is the whole
# reach. 22 is outside it and 10 is inside.
#
# The second half is a control, and it is the half that makes the first half
# worth anything. A refused aim would also read green if the gizmo never opened
# a targeter at all, or if the label were wrong - the test would be green for
# the wrong reason forever. So the same gizmo is pressed again at a cell inside
# the range, that aim has to be taken, and the decoy has to stand there
# afterwards. Green on both lines means the route works and the range is what
# separated them.
#
# On a kit without expect= on "target" this file goes red, not green: the older
# handler treats a targeter that is still asking as a failure. A key cannot be
# held back by "requires", so the loud failure is the safeguard.

requires dlc=Biotech
requires dlc=Royalty
requires verb=ability

despawn Thing:BX_DarkMirageDecoy
spawn Pawn:Colonist at 0,0 name="Plain"
ability "Plain" grant=BX_DarkMirage psylink=2 psyfocus=1.0

# disableGizmoWhileUndrafted is true on the def, so an undrafted pawn offers the
# gizmo greyed out and ProcessInput would never open a targeter.
draft "Plain"

# "gizmo" reads the gizmo bar of the selection, so the caster has to be selected.
select "Plain"
assert thing BX_DarkMirageDecoy expect=absent

# 22 is outside the 19.9 the def writes. The targeter has to keep asking.
gizmo "Dark mirage"
target cell=22,0 expect=refused

# The control: 10 is inside the range, over open ground, so line of sight holds
# and the same aim has to be taken.
gizmo "Dark mirage"
target cell=10,0

# warmupTime is 0.6 s, so 36 ticks, and the job has to walk nowhere. 90 is that
# plus margin - this line is not decoration here the way it is behind "cast",
# because this route really does run a job and a warmup.
tick 90 reason="0.6 s warmup is 36 ticks, plus the job that carries it"

assert thing BX_DarkMirageDecoy at 10,0

undraft "Plain"
assert log clean
